Chapter: E1000TxDeadline
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Hpet

 The transmit wait against a descriptor the hardware never completes. No
 device is involved: the subject reads a status byte out of memory, so a
 scratch address with that byte clear is exactly the case where a card has
 taken the frame and not reported it done, and it needs no fault injection
 to produce.

 What this pins is that the wait is bounded by the CLOCK and not by an
 iteration count. Measured 2026-08-14, one million iterations of that loop
 shape cost 605 microseconds on this box, so the bare `e1000-tx-fuel` spin
 it used until then was a 605 microsecond budget. A 1500-byte frame takes
 1200 microseconds on the wire at 10 Mb/s, so the budget expired before the
 frame could leave and `e1000-send-frame` returns this value directly: every
 send on a slow link reported failure while the frame went out anyway.

 The judge is a BAND because a duration is not reproducible, and the control
 below is the old spin path measured on the same descriptor in the same run.
 The two bands do not overlap and cannot: that is what makes this an arm
 rather than a restatement.

Section: Fixtures

  scratch : Integer = e1000-alloc-aligned 64 16

  elapsed-ms : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  elapsed-ms (t0) (t1) =
   let rate = hpet-ticks-per-second
   in if rate <= 0 then -1 else (t1 - t0) * 1000 / rate

  in-band : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  in-band (ms) (lo) (hi) = if ms >= lo & ms <= hi then "in band" else "out of band"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let z = poke-32 (scratch + 12) 0 0
    in let started = hpet-start
    in let c0 = hpet-ticks
    in let clocked = e1000-await-tx scratch
    in let c1 = hpet-ticks
    in let s0 = hpet-ticks
    in let spun = e1000-await-tx-spin scratch 0
    in let s1 = hpet-ticks
    in act
      print-line-uni ("clocked gave up : " & (if clocked == 0 then "yes" else "no"))
      print-line-uni ("clocked ms      : " & in-band (elapsed-ms c0 c1) 10 200)
      print-line-uni ("control gave up : " & (if spun == 0 then "yes" else "no"))
      print-line-uni ("control ms      : " & in-band (elapsed-ms s0 s1) 0 5)
    end
  end

